.TH SWAYDESK-CAPTURE 1 2026-11-14 "swaydesk 0.1.3" "Sway desktop components"
.SH NAME
swaydesk\-capture \- screenshot and screen recording panels
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swaydesk\-capture
shot
.br
.B swaydesk\-capture
rec
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens a panel in the middle of the screen to choose what to capture. The keys are English initials: r Region, s Screen, w Window, g Gradia (when it is installed), d Delay, a Audio. In the recording panel, Shift with a key records the system sound and Ctrl the microphone. The sway\-shot and sway\-rec helpers take the picture or record, after the panel closes.
.PP
The shortcut of the same panel closes it, and the shortcut of the other one switches panels; Esc or clicking outside closes it.
.PP
The session runs it under the name sway\-capture (a link in the package's helper directory to /usr/bin/swaydesk\-capture); the process name is sway\-capture too.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B shot
The screenshot panel.
.TP
.B rec
The screen recording panel; while recording, it stops the recording.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Exit 0 at once without doing anything: the Python launchers use it to check that the binary and its libraries load.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/sway\-capture.json
The last choices (Gradia and audio).
.TP
.I ~/.config/sway\-desktop/config.toml
The desktop configuration: language, accent color, GTK and icon themes, folder color, file manager, weather location and holidays.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grim (1),
.BR slurp (1),
.BR swaydesk (7),
.BR wf\-recorder (1)
